    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "callout_0",
      "quote": "Previous studies have identified diabetes as an independent risk factor for poor prognosis of coronavirus disease-2019 (COVID-19). Diabetes is a complex disease with different degrees of severity. However, some of the findings are still conflicting, imprecisely estimated or affected by risk of bias, such as confounding.",
      "reason": "Describes current knowledge on diabetes as a risk factor and uncertainties due to conflicting findings and bias."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "callout_0",
      "quote": "To provide the best available evidence for the identification of risk phenotypes of diabetes in association with COVID-19 severity and death, a systematic review and meta-analysis is needed that summarises the findings, reveals more robust estimates, considers risk of bias and evaluates the certainty of evidence.",
      "reason": "Explains the need for the review to summarize evidence and address limitations of single studies."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "callout_0",
      "quote": "Several systematic reviews and meta-analyses on diabetes and COVID-19 prognosis have observed an approximately two- to threefold increased risk of mortality due to COVID-19 for people with diabetes compared with people without diabetes [6 - 14]. However, diabetes is a complex and heterogeneous disease... To provide the best available evidence... a systematic review and meta-analysis is needed...",
      "reason": "Cites previous reviews and explains the need for the current review to address complexity and provide updated evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review focuses on observational studies of risk phenotypes, not intervention effects, so the element does not apply."
    },
    {
